# tls_messages.dict - what tls/messages.asm and tls/extensions.asm compare against (libFuzzer
# cannot see it in NASM code): every extension type the walk knows (its index table, the three
# above 255 by compare), whole empty extensions of the types that must be empty, the versions
# supported_versions lists (0x0304 makes a ClientHello a TLS 1.3 offer), the groups and suites
# and signature schemes of RFC 8448's traces, record_size_limit's floor (64) and one under it,
# the HelloRetryRequest random (SHA-256 of "HelloRetryRequest"), and ALPN's protocol names.
